n" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/da6c0fb32e62b6effe133c527fee528c47b6f1c8dc7dd1d77d7d04f42b4c3d2b.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the quadrilateral shown above under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nSince $T$ is the zero matrix, the image of our object under the action of $T$ is the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3117cac283fb94cc19d5fe97a6acc1c3e0354b103cbb0237db3b15f187694112" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A line segment"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A point, different from the origin"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A quadrilateral"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A triangle"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/e6d0ce147aec90c3840a893e36596fbadf981ff96559f65d055f4486406cca7f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the quadrilateral shown above under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a nonsingular matrix. Therefore, the image of our object under the action of  $T$ is a quadrilateral." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3117cac283fb94cc19d5fe97a6acc1c3e0354b103cbb0237db3b15f187694112" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A line segment"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A point, different from the origin"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A quadrilateral"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A triangle"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "14476014320fedf4d1a6acd7b6131a6a9a2aeec40dc6c5bc972ee7ec8ac4d420" "basis" 1050 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/27c1ad7d429eb8da46b0bb3baec048b3564ce206b4523416cb4cb56b0a33767f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(3,-6)$, $(0,0),$ $(6,-12).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/9c045d6467a91676cd27a4c11cbb651a798b2480662d09b446b52d8eeb490ff4.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41bb6ac81580a35044f519df3893ae599125755be510d24cfbe36d3329447b5e" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147611" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147611" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/69e3e6eabe9e2ea5d28a6ff0feb40437965649af45ad247b572a35ac3bf642a4.png"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147611" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/9c045d6467a91676cd27a4c11cbb651a798b2480662d09b446b52d8eeb490ff4.png"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147611" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/d271c5f4cf0f250dcfdbba8addfdc5f8c583832f378756fc3066e2b961a31dc3.png"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147611" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/d38c8f370e25add2a06ecc652127bae817e2c8bc394f4db6fdf539fbfef3750c.png"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-147611" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/f9040d78661e0d33290ad14e1ddf815211985f5963c8e1c8b9b5438dd8f3931c.png"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/e6d0ce147aec90c3840a893e36596fbadf981ff96559f65d055f4486406cca7f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the quadrilateral shown above under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a nonsingular matrix. Therefore, the image of our object under the action of  $T$ is a quadrilateral." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41bb6ac81580a35044f519df3893ae599125755be510d24cfbe36d3329447b5e" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A line segment"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A point, different from the origin"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A quadrilateral"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A triangle"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162206" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A quadrilateral"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/state.json" "file_sha256" "0348ac96e75cda8bea4605b4f31c845ce938f1dac84389d538fb21fc11dcf459" "basis" 2012 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-21058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072249/assets/fee79ec0b214a4ba87400b4b8c9dab2c623878d067821c572b26ae241625c48a.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072249/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c22ed54c149cdad52322e7cf331176a4947a719e830f80b32cb94b53b2ef772"} {"question" "q-21058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 15 & 25\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(2,10)$, $(3,15)$, and  $(5,25).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072249/assets/bf5987fde11416780a6a599e3952db7319e1c0e859e2439b7df70c5659bc6839.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072249/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c22ed54c149cdad52322e7cf331176a4947a719e830f80b32cb94b53b2ef772"} {"question" "q-21058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072249/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dd6d254fe764e51546faa30c13340e0b9fbe5c3f48caba75e8395c53810475e7"} {"question" "q-21058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072249/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c22ed54c149cdad52322e7cf331176a4947a719e830f80b32cb94b53b2ef772"} {"question" "q-21058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072249/assets/1a027e19617c0c62fd8f5247c6d1bbac894f9522ec9e90aec5b7ed05b3996b37.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072249/assets/52266ff97300b29c85ac14f5b60b308d9e8a0e2fe3a01e8e0431b643e6a28922.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072249/assets/cac3c2b4fb6191aa9a523b445d8533774f438d24556ea79b8e67a4d6c3867526.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072249/assets/e667849ed8a214e7d17871b0f